{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And Jacob took for himself rods of fresh poplar.</b> And if you ask: Jacob was a complete righteous man — how did he act deceptively? There is an answer: Jacob said to Laban in his condition: remove from there every speckled and spotted lamb and every brown one among the sheep, etc. — he meant the young ones, so that people would not say they are stolen from me; but the grown ones he did not tell him to remove, so that they would produce offspring like themselves. And he changed the condition and removed even the grown ones, as it is written: ״ויסר ביום ההוא את התישים״ etc. — even the grown ones. Therefore Jacob did everything he could do. And further, the sage Rabbi Chaim says: Laban changed his condition — he had not stipulated to remove anything but the speckled ones, yet he removed even the ring-streaked ones; therefore he set up the rods, as it is written: ״ועם עקש תתפל״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:21.992122829Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}